# PINN Review Atlas Licensing Policy

Copyright (c) 2026 PINN Review Atlas contributors.

PINN Review Atlas is a mixed research-software repository. No single license applies to every file or every element of every file.

## 1. Atlas software and code — MIT License

Original software and code authored for PINN Review Atlas are licensed under the MIT License. See [LICENSES/MIT.txt](LICENSES/MIT.txt).

This includes, to the extent authored for the Atlas:

- `scripts/**`;
- JavaScript, ECMAScript modules, CSS, Python, and other executable source under `assets/**`, `docs/**`, and other repository paths;
- software logic contained in the Atlas HTML pages and interactive tools;
- Atlas build, validation, data-processing, user-interface, and automation code; and
- repository workflow/configuration code under `.github/**`, where copyright applies.

For mixed HTML or other mixed-content files, the MIT License applies to the software implementation, while Atlas-authored prose, scientific descriptions, curated annotations, and data content are governed by Section 2 below.

## 2. Atlas-authored research content, curated data, and documentation — CC BY 4.0

Original non-software material authored or curated for PINN Review Atlas is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0). See [LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt](LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt).

This includes, to the extent original to the Atlas:

- curated annotations and classifications;
- taxonomies, controlled vocabularies, canonical concept mappings, and normalized labels;
- Atlas-authored relationships among methods, formulations, metrics, software, concepts, and papers;
- Atlas-authored scientific descriptions, explanatory text, documentation, diagrams, and data dictionaries;
- curated country, method, optimizer, activation-function, performance-metric, formulation, ecosystem, and related research-data products;
- Atlas-derived summaries, validation outputs, quality-control records, and provenance structures; and
- Atlas-authored portions of `README.md`, `docs/**`, `data/**`, and the public site content.

The CC BY 4.0 grant applies only to material for which the PINN Review Atlas contributors hold the relevant rights.

## 3. Third-party material is not relicensed

Third-party material is excluded from the MIT and CC BY 4.0 grants unless an explicit notice states otherwise.

This includes, where present:

- article abstracts and other publication text;
- publisher-provided or author-provided graphical abstracts, figures, images, or supplementary material;
- third-party bibliographic, citation, DOI, venue, publisher, or publication metadata to the extent protected by applicable rights;
- third-party source excerpts and imported data;
- external publications and datasets linked from the Atlas;
- third-party software, libraries, map data, logos, marks, and other assets; and
- material carrying its own license, terms of use, or public-domain status.

Such material remains subject to the rights, licenses, terms, and exceptions applicable to its original source. See [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICE.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICE.md).

Factual information may not be protected by copyright in some jurisdictions. Nothing in this policy is intended to claim rights in facts or public-domain material.

## 4. Mixed datasets and mixed files

Some Atlas files combine original Atlas contributions with third-party source material. Examples include bibliographic records that combine Atlas identifiers, normalization, curation, provenance, and derived fields with publication metadata or abstract text.

In those cases:

- the Atlas-authored selection, organization, annotations, normalization, relationships, and other original contributions are licensed under CC BY 4.0;
- the software used to build, validate, transform, or display the material is licensed under MIT; and
- third-party elements retain their original legal status and are not relicensed by this repository.

A downstream user is responsible for identifying and complying with any rights that apply to excluded third-party elements.

## 5. Specific notices take precedence

If a file or directory contains a more specific license, attribution, public-domain statement, or third-party notice, that specific notice controls for the material it identifies.

For example, `data/world-map.json` has separate provenance documented in `data/world-map-attribution.md`.

## 6. Trademarks and endorsement

Copyright licenses in this repository do not grant trademark rights or imply endorsement by PINN Review Atlas, any publisher, any author, or any third party.

